  {
    "reviewId": 16961747,
    "trailId": 10571725,
    "comment": "This is a beautiful trail to take to visit the three falls: Tiffany fall, Sherman fall and Canterbury fall. The parking near Tiffany fall is right off the road. It can take up to 20+ cars, my guess. Parking is good for only one hour on weekends but not restricted during weekdays. There’s another parking at Sherman fall, but it’s supposed to be smaller and busier, as Sherman fall is more popular. Parking limitation aside, the trail is very nice. You just follow the white blaze (main trail) for Bruce trail. Not challenging and not long (round trip is about 7 km). You want to be careful and stay on the trail because the surroundings are private property. There are shades most of the time. It’s not crowded on a Friday. Sherman fall is definitely the most impressive one but Tiffany fall is decent too. Canterbury fall is the least impressive as a fall but the wood it’s located in is quite refreshing. Overall, if you can figure out the parking limitation or do it on a weekday, highly recommended!",
    "date": "2021-08-20T15:19:22.000Z",
